;; spec:   stdlib §2.5 (a bulk vec builds the trie in one pass), §8.1 item 5 (count cases)
;; expect: accept
;; result: 64
;; audit:  clean
;; allocs: <= 15
;; roots:  ../../lib support
;; covers: vec
;; vec of an Array of 64 elements: the walk's default to-vec, which is the bulk builder (L9). The same
;; program allocated 133 objects with the conj loop that was the default before (2.09 an element, measured
;; with the compiler built before the builder); it allocates 15 now, and the bound is the count: one
;; more object fails it, and the harness's own test lowers it by one and requires the failure. The
;; array is an `(array n x)`, one object the trace counts. Case 489 pins the builder's constant on a
;; vector of three, 490 and 491 the order of growth.
(ns main (:use fib.core fib.seq fib.coll))

(defun main () -> i64
  (let ((v (vec (array 64 0))))
    (count v)))
